{
  "$schema": "../family.schema.json",
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "id": "hip-hinge",
  "name": "Hip Hinge",
  "definition": "A bilateral unsupported closed-chain barbell good morning in which the athlete begins upright with a free bar across the posterior shoulder and upper-back surface, hinges through a reviewed control-limited range, and returns to standing through combined hip and spinal extension. The roster preserves Schellenberg et al.'s exact eight-repetition fixture with shoulder-width, slightly toe-out feet and external barbell load equal to 25 percent of body mass, and adds an everyday high-bar strength fixture using Ross et al.'s approximately hip-width stance, forward or slightly toe-out feet, equidistant overhand grip, slight maintained knee bend, and program-selected external load. Vigotsky et al. directly measured trained lifters across 50 to 90 percent of estimated one-repetition maximum without prescribing depth or tempo; their load-dependent increase in knee flexion is treated as an observed limitation, not an authored technique cue. The everyday record's controlled self-selected tempo and control-limited depth are explicit catalog safety boundaries rather than source-measured cadence or depth. Both experimental sources measured lumbar or segmental excursion, so spinal extension remains explicit rather than being hidden behind a neutral-spine coaching cue. Medial hamstrings, gluteus maximus, and lumbar extensors are non-ranked co-primary contributors. The visible biceps-femoris region receives only knee-control credit because its unsplit mesh cannot distinguish the hip-extending long head from the monoarticular short head. Romanian, stiff-leg, conventional, sumo, trap-bar, deficit, unilateral, staggered, dumbbell, cable, Smith, floor-pull, swing, and externally supported back-extension variants remain outside this contract.",
  "evidenceRefs": [
    "arnold-2010-lower-limb",
    "christophy-2012-lumbar-spine",
    "schellenberg-2013-deadlift-goodmorning-kinematics",
    "ross-2024-good-morning-technique",
    "vigotsky-2015-good-morning-load"
  ],
